## File path

`G:\PROJECT1\KasirKu\src\app\business\[businessId]\(dashboard)\ticket-reports\export\route.ts`

(A sibling exists at `reports/export/route.ts` with a similar pattern, not read here since the task named ticket-reports.)

## 1. CSV building

Manual string building via two small helpers, no library:

```ts
function csvEscape(v: string | number | null | undefined) {
  const s = String(v ?? "");
  return s.includes(",") || s.includes('"') || s.includes("\n")
    ? `"${s.replace(/"/g, '""')}"`
    : s;
}

function toCsv(rows: (string | number)[][]) {
  return rows.map((r) => r.map(csvEscape).join(",")).join("\r\n");
}
```

Rows are built as `(string | number)[][]`, first row is the header. A UTF-8 BOM is prepended before serving:

```ts
return new Response(String.fromCharCode(0xfeff) + toCsv(rows), { ... });
```

(comment: `// BOM (U+FEFF) supaya Excel membuka file sebagai UTF-8.`)

## 2. Headers

```ts
return new Response(String.fromCharCode(0xfeff) + toCsv(rows), {
  headers: {
    "Content-Type": "text/csv; charset=utf-8",
    "Content-Disposition": `attachment; filename="${filename}"`,
  },
});
```

Filename pattern: `` `TiketTransaksi_${periodLabel}.csv` `` (also `TiketPerUnit_...` / `TiketPerJam_...`), where `periodLabel` is `fmtDate(new Date().toISOString()).replace(/\//g, "-")` for `period === "today"`, else the raw period string.

## 3. Route type & invocation

It's a `GET` route handler (`export async function GET(request, { params })`), reading query params via `new URL(request.url).searchParams` (`type`, `period`, `from`, `to`, `category`, `serialFrom`, `serialTo`).

Invoked from the UI as a plain anchor link (no JS/fetch), e.g. in `ticket-reports/page.tsx` line 430-434:

```tsx
<a href={`/business/${businessId}/ticket-reports/export?type=transactions&${periodQuery}`}>
  🧾 Transaksi
</a>
```

Browser navigation to the GET URL triggers the download via `Content-Disposition: attachment`.
